@@ -21,3 +21,15 @@ how it was checked. Drop a patch once the submodule moves past its fix.
   without it: ZyperOS's mk/dsperate-extbg-check.sh (96 frames of bitmaps,
   direct colour and tile maps in four bank layouts) and Pokemon Black frames
   from a saved state.
+- `0004-two-bands-under-layout.patch` - under the thread layout the CPU
+  raster draws in two bands again, one beside each 2D engine, as before
+  DSperate a6f2e935 added a third on the aux core. In a libretro frontend
+  that core carries the frontend's present, audio and input threads at
+  normal priority, and the band's SCHED_RR pre-empted them: on a GKD Pixel 2
+  with ZyperOS's Diatom, from the same saved states, the panel showed 56.6
+  fps in a Mario Kart DS race and 53.5 in Pokemon Black with three bands,
+  59.8 in both with two, at the same core time, 11.3 ms a frame
+  (2026-11-16). The third band on another core gained nothing (beside the
+  2D engines) or cost Mario Kart 2.8 ms a frame (beside the emulation
+  thread). `DS_R3D_BANDS=n` still overrides. A raster with a VBlank
+  deadline (Guitar Hero: On Tour with CPU AA) does without the third band.
